        <headline>Small Craft Advisory issued September 25 at 3:05AM EDT until September 26 at 2:00PM EDT by NWS Charleston SC</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...For the Gale Warning, north winds around 25 kt with
gusts up to 35 kt and seas 8 to 10 ft. For the Small Craft
Advisory, north winds 15 to 25 kt with gusts up to 35 kt and
seas 7 to 10 ft expected.

* WHERE...Savannah to Altamaha Sound from 20 to 60 NM.

* WHEN...For the Gale Warning, until 6 AM EDT early this
morning. For the Small Craft Advisory, until 2 PM EDT Saturday.

* IMPACTS...Strong winds will cause hazardous seas which could
capsize or damage vessels and reduce visibility.
</description>
        <instruction>Mariners should alter plans to avoid these hazardous conditions.
Remain in port, seek safe harbor, alter course, and/or secure the
vessel for hazardous conditions.</instruction>
